WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:03.837
[music playing]

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.338
- Oh, [bleep]!

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.874
Go this way, go this way.

00:00:07.941 --> 00:00:10.744
Ease, ease.

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.078
Oh, yeah.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.013
A bear had been going through
here digging up bee nests.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.548
Oh, another one over there!

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:21.654
I see bear markings on
the trees back here, too.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.857
So if other bears are coming
through, they smell this

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:27.093
and they know he's the
bear that owns this place.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.830
See he chewed up the
tree on this side?

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.432
See, this his marking post.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.801
It goes all the way up there.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.736
He's probably around
here, because you

00:00:36.803 --> 00:00:39.906
see all those fresh marks where
he dug up those yellow jackets.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.107
He's right around here.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.244
[music playing]

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.979
This doesn't factor
into my choice

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.314
too much where I'm going to
put the camp because there's

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.616
bears everywhere around here.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.851
But it's going to be pretty
sketchy sleeping at night.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.657
But where I make my camp, I'm
going to determine by where

00:00:57.724 --> 00:00:59.959
is the best access from
the river to the lake,

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.628
and seeing this big
animal trail here

00:01:01.694 --> 00:01:03.863
tells me that the moose
used this spot because it's

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.565
the easiest place to
walk back and forth

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.933
from the lake to the river.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.136
So what I'm thinking is this
is a prime spot to make camp.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.473
[shimmer, music playing]

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.374
OK, Sky.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.276
Let's get this tarp.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.977
Just spread it out
as far as you can.

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.079
See we're going to put it
between these trees here,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:21.481
and this is just
going to give us

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.117
a nice little dry spot we
could sit under or even

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.985
leave our firewood here.

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.988
Let's try to get this
done before the rain hits.

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:33.593
We might be using this tarp
before we even know it.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.095
It's about two weeks out
from moose hunting season,

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:38.731
but it takes a lot of work,
and it takes a lot of noise

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:40.166
to put up a moose hunting camp.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.669
And I want to do this early so
I'm not making all that noise

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.405
and having to do all this
work during moose hunting.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:46.773
- We could set a wall tent here.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.841
- Yeah.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.342
Well, this is something
we could leave up.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:50.577
We don't even have
to take it down.

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.545
We don't want to put a
wall tent up and walk away.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.548
A bear might tear
the crap out of it.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:57.450
This is a big step for
Skylar because he's

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:59.118
hunted a lot of small
game, but now he's

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.720
got to think of
the bigger animals,

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.889
and it's a lot more
dangerous hunting big game.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.624
So he's going to have
to stick close to me

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.993
and learn all these different
moves we do out here to try

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.729
to get a good opportunity
to harvest something,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:11.664
so it's exciting for him.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.935
And now we'll stand it up.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:21.641
OK, tarp's up.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.376
Beautiful view of
the river right here.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.211
If any moose come out,
you'll be able to see

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.113
him on the bar from here.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:30.049
A little bit of gas money,
some hard work, and this

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:33.586
is how we put food on the
table out here in Alaska.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.990
[music playing]

